From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:22:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wip(F30#0): host rolls ordinary wild traits; canonical
 catches retain them (verification running)

Not for landing yet: catch smokes with the flag on are still running.

- encounter_director.foundation_stamp_wild_traits: the host rolls
  Traits.roll_spawn once at registration from (world namespace, realm +
  body name + process epoch, generation), with the alpha and night/weather
  profiles. Guests never roll. The cluster rng is untouched (test_shiny).
  A refill bumps the generation.
- _host_catch_finished: an ordinary canonical body's packet becomes the
  catch's capture_traits, and session.foundation_wild_capture_offer
  journals the same capture_offer FoundationEvent an alpha uses
  (exactly-once install, initialize_caught, reconnect).
- foundation_capture and _foundation_capture_context no longer require
  alpha_respawns.runtime_enabled: a retained valid offer is its own
  authorization.
- The legacy local catch strips a transient stamp (it keeps legacy
  trait_primary adoption); it retires with the legacy path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
